Objects that Consume Disk Space

Objects that consume disk space include datasets, timeflows, and snapshots. 

        Delphix storage is primarily consumed by datasets (including dSources and VDBs) and their associated timeflows and snapshots.


        A timeflow represents the timeline/history of a dataset, and snapshots represent the state of that dataset at specific points in time.


you can access capacity information for the Delphix Engine through several different means, including the Dashboard view, and the Storage Capacity screen.

